   "text": "The pattern looks like two phases: **SrLu2O4 (mp-756646) plus BaNdCuBO5 (mp-10350)**. The second phase fits less cleanly than the first.\n\nI read peak positions by counting grid points in the intensity list. I miscounted once near 40\u00b0 and corrected it, so positions above about 40\u00b0 carry some uncertainty.\n\n**SrLu2O4 spinel (cubic a \u2248 9.64 \u00c5).** All its expected reflections in range are matched:\n- (111) at about 15.95\u00b0\n- (311) at about 30.8\u00b0\n- (222) at about 32.1\u00b0\n- (400) at about 37.25\u00b0\n- (422) at about 46.1\u00b0\n- (511) at about 49.15\u00b0\n- (440) at about 53.8\u00b0\n\n**Peaks the spinel does not explain.** These are at about 11.5\u00b0 (weak), 22.55\u00b0, 23.15\u00b0 (weak), 32.5\u00b0 (the strongest peak), 39.95\u00b0, 47.3\u00b0 and 51.8\u00b0.\n\n**BaNdCuBO5 (a = 5.555 \u00c5, c = 7.658 \u00c5) as the second phase.**\n- It explains most of the remaining peaks:\n  - (001) at 11.55\u00b0\n  - (110) at 22.62\u00b0\n  - (002) at 23.2\u00b0\n  - (112) at 32.63\u00b0, matching the strongest peak\n  - (202) at 40.07\u00b0\n  - (004) at 47.45\u00b0\n- Its (220) at 46.2\u00b0 would overlap the spinel (422).\n- Two points weaken this fit. The peak at about 51.8\u00b0 falls between its predicted (213) at 51.3\u00b0 and (222) at 52.3\u00b0. Its (201) and (210) reflections, near 34.3\u00b0 and 36.1\u00b0, are not seen.\n\n**Other candidates ruled out.**\n- Ba2Nd(CuO2)3 would put a strong (103) peak at about 31.7\u00b0, and none is observed.\n- BaSrMn2O6, BaSrCaWO6, K2O, RbAgO, LiMnO2 and CaGe2O5 all predict peaks at positions that are absent from the pattern.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-756646\", \"mp-10350\"], \"confidence\": 0.65, \"note\": \"Spinel SrLu2O4 accounts for the 15.95/30.8/32.1/37.25/46.1/49.15/53.8 degree peaks, and BaNdCuBO5 best fits the remaining 11.5/22.55/23.15/32.5/39.95/47.3 degree peaks, though its 51.8 degree match is imperfect.\"}",
